// Seven-Card Stud — formalized DSL (parser/checker/runtime target).
//
// Companion to seven-card-stud.md. Fixed-limit Seven-Card Stud, the corpus's
// first betting game. Chips are modelled as an integer `stack` per player (not a
// resource-zone subsystem). Each player antes, the low door card brings in, and
// five betting streets (3rd–7th) precede a showdown where the best five-of-seven
// poker hand takes the pot (with side pots for all-ins). The .md models a cash
// game with no overall winner; to give the runtime a terminal, this plays until
// one player holds all the chips and declares that player the winner.
//
// The betting runs on the kernel `round`'s ring: the pointer advances past
// whoever just acted, so the seats behind the aggressor decide before the
// seats its bet re-opened — poker's continuation order. `until` is checked
// before every draw, so a street closes the moment nobody is pending rather
// than at the end of a lap.
//
// THE BRING-IN POSTER HOLDS THE OPTION — this variant's own rule, pinned here
// because no authority settles it. Called around, the seat that posted the
// bring-in may raise its own post as well as check, exactly as Hold'em's big
// blind may: the library reaches it because a post placed before the round
// begins is not a turn taken within it (decisions.md, "Named functions"), and
// nothing the library can read separates the two forced posts. Pagat, fetched
// live, describes only the SUBSEQUENT players' rights ("subsequent players have
// the option to complete the bet to a small bet ($5), to call the bring-in ($2)
// or to fold") and is silent on the poster's own later turn, on the variant page
// and on poker/rules/betting.html alike — where the big blind's option is
// spelled out. So this is a choice, made once and recorded, not a rule quoted
// from a source. What the poster's raise COSTS is Pagat's own ladder: the
// bring-in is 2, completing it makes the bet 5 — the street's size, not the
// bring-in plus it — and a raise from there makes it 10.
//
// Antes, the deal, the bring-in post, the five streets, and the showdown (a
// contested hand's reveal, the per-entrant pot collection, the muck) are all DSL
// statements; the bring-in / best-showing seat selectors and the `pot_share`
// side-pot query are Primitives (argmin over door cards; argmax over the
// showing-hand order and over poker-rank tuples). The poker evaluator is
// unit-tested. Chips are plain integers.
//
// Both selectors are anchored on the CARDS, never on the chips: a seat left
// with nothing by the ante still shows a door card and can be the bring-in, and
// an all-in seat can hold the best board a later street opens on. What such a
// seat posts is what it has, and the round's own `pending` filter walks the
// action to the first seat clockwise that can act.
//
// THE OPEN-PAIR BIG BET. From 4th street on, a pair showing opens the big bet
// to every active player — as an OPTION beside the small bet, not in place of
// it: "big bets ($10) are allowed if any player has a pair (or better)
// showing. In this case anyone can place a big bet or raise, even if they do
// not themselves have a pair." 4th street therefore opens at TWO sizes when a
// pair shows, and a seat choosing to wager picks between them. 5th street on is
// big-bet-only here (see THE VARIANT below), so 4th is the only street the rule
// changes.
//
// THE VARIANT, which the page offers rather than states. Two of Pagat's options
// are taken here, and both are the casino form:
//
//   The limit ladder is 5/5/10/10/10 — "Some play that from fifth street
//   onwards, only big bets are allowed. This is the normal rule in casino
//   hosted games, but not in home poker games."
//
//   `big_raise_only` is true — "if the rule is played that each raise must be
//   at least as large as the last bet or raise, then after a player places a
//   big bet, only big raises are allowed in that round. However, many home
//   poker games do not have this rule". The library carries both arms; this
//   file names the one it plays.
//
// The ratchet keys on a big wager being PLACED, not on the standing bet
// reaching the big size: a street that climbs to 10 through two small wagers
// has seen no big bet, and the small raise is still open there.

game SevenCardStud {

  // Betting proceeds as in standard fixed-limit poker: check/bet/call/raise and
  // the ring predicates come from the family library shared with Kuhn and Leduc
  // (docs/libraries/poker_betting.cardlang). `fold` is Stud's own — it mucks the
  // folder's upcards, which is a fact about Stud's zones, not about betting.
  uses poker_betting

  players: 4
  direction: clockwise
  max_length: 30000

  cards: standard52
  ranking: aces high

  // What this game borrows from outside the DSL, implemented in
  // `cardlang/runtime/stud.py`: the door-card seat selectors and the
  // showdown's side-pot query. Each entry declares what its own implementation
  // consults, so the clauses differ — the bring-in is chosen before anyone can
  // fold, and the settlement reads no stack, because what it returns is what
  // moves one.
  //
  // `committed`, `folded` and `in_hand` are declared by `phase play`, not by
  // the game, so a read of one names that phase. The tail rides the READ, not
  // the clause: `stack` is game-level and carries none. Naming the phase also
  // promises what the resolver then checks — an entry reading `in play` is
  // called only where `play` is running, which here is the phase's own body
  // and the streets' round configurations.
  primitives {
    bring_in_seat() : Player
        reads upcards
    best_showing_seat() : Player
        reads folded in play, upcards
    pot_share(p : Player) : Integer
        reads committed in play, folded in play, in_hand in play, hole, upcards
  }

  zones {
    deck            : Deck
    hole[player]    : Hand<player>           // face-down cards
    upcards[player] : PublicHand<player>     // face-up cards
    muck            : Muck                   // folded / spent cards
    burn            : Burn                   // one burned card per street
  }

  state {
    // Chips as integers; total is invariant. The winner holds them all.
    stack[player] : Integer = 100
  }

  phase hand_sequence repeat until (number of players where stack[player] > 0) <= 1 {
    state {
      dealer : Player = 0
    }

    before_each {
      move all cards to deck
      shuffle deck
      dealer := dealer offset_by left
    }

    phase play {
      state {
        // Per-hand betting state, reset each hand on phase re-entry. `acted`
        // and `limit` are not here because poker_betting provides them: they
        // live at game level and carry across hands, which is harmless because
        // every street opens with `open_street`, and a hand that opens no
        // street (everyone all-in on the ante) runs no round and reads
        // neither.
        in_hand[player]   : Boolean = false   // entered the hand holding chips
        committed[player] : Integer = 0       // chips put in this hand (for side pots)
        folded[player]    : Boolean = false
        bet_by[player]    : Integer = 0        // chips put in on the current street
        bet_to_match      : Integer = 0        // the street's standing bet
        level             : Integer = 0        // the last FULL wager this street
        raises            : Integer = 0        // raises so far on this street
        raise_cap         : Integer = 4        // a bet and three raises
        big_raise_only    : Boolean = true    // the casino arm: a big wager withdraws the small raise
      }

      // Snapshot the entrants (held chips); ante and deal follow this set.
      for each player p: in_hand[p] := stack[p] > 0

      // Antes: every entrant posts one chip (entrants hold >= 1, so never partial).
      for each player p: if in_hand[p] {
        stack[p] := stack[p] - 1
        committed[p] := committed[p] + 1
      }

      // Deal two hole + one upcard, grouped per entrant (the monolith pop order:
      // each player takes three off the top before the next).
      for each player p: if in_hand[p] {
        deal 2 cards from deck to hole[p]
        deal 1 card from deck to upcards[p]
      }

      // Bring-in + 3rd street. Skipped only when fewer than two entrants can act
      // (everyone all-in on the ante); then the hand is dealt straight to showdown.
      if (number of players where stack[player] > 0) >= 2 {
        run open_street(5, 0)
        let bringer = bring_in_seat()
        // The bring-in is a forced post (no decision): the lowest door puts 2 — a
        // partial all-in if it holds only one chip — and stands as the opening bet.
        // It posts AFTER the street is opened, so opening does not clear it.
        //
        // It spends none of the street's aggressions, and neither does the
        // completion that follows it. Robert's Rules of Seven-Card Stud 3:
        // "Increasing the amount wagered by the opening forced bet up to a full
        // bet does not count as a raise, but merely as a completion of the bet.
        // For example: In $15-$30 stud, the lowcard opens for $5. If the next
        // player increases the bet to $15 (completes the bet), up to three
        // raises are then allowed when using a three-raise limit." So `raises`
        // stays where `open_street` put it: the library counts the street's
        // first FULL wager, which is the completion, and the book's three
        // raises then fit under a cap of four.
        bet_by[bringer] := if 2 < stack[bringer] then 2 else stack[bringer]
        stack[bringer] := stack[bringer] - bet_by[bringer]
        committed[bringer] := committed[bringer] + bet_by[bringer]
        bet_to_match := bet_by[bringer]
        round offering [check, bet, call, fold, raise] from bringer offset_by left
              over players where pending(player)
              until (number of players where pending(player)) is 0
                 or ((number of players where can_act(player)) <= 1
                     and (number of players where can_act(player) and owes(player)) is 0)
      }

      // 4th–7th streets: burn, deal one card, then a betting round (limits 5/10/10/10;
      // 7th is dealt face down). Each street runs only while more than one contender
      // remains. The contender count is monotonic (folds only add, in_hand is fixed),
      // so once it drops to one every later street's guard short-circuits — the four
      // streets are written flat, not nested, with identical behaviour. The ring
      // filter and terminator are factored into the named functions below; folding
      // the repeated round *block* into one loop is still open (no list/street
      // loop) — see open-questions/round-config-factoring.md.

      // 4th street (face up, lower limit — and the street the open-pair rule
      // reaches). "From fourth street onward, big bets ($10) are allowed if any
      // player has a pair (or better) showing. In this case anyone can place a
      // big bet or raise, even if they do not themselves have a pair." Allowed,
      // not compulsory: where a pair shows, BOTH sizes are legal and a seat
      // choosing to wager picks between them, so the street opens at two sizes
      // rather than switching to one. Where none shows, the second size is 0
      // and the street is the small-bet street it always was.
      //
      // 5th street on is big-bet-only under this file's variant, so the rule
      // has nothing left to open there — this is the one street it changes.
      if (number of players where in_hand[player] and not folded[player]) > 1 {
        deal 1 card from deck to burn
        for each player p: if in_hand[p] and not folded[p] { deal 1 card from deck to upcards[p] }
        if (number of players where can_act(player)) >= 2 {
          run open_street(5, if (number of players where shows_pair(player)) > 0 then 10 else 0)
          round offering [check, bet, bet_big, call, fold, raise, raise_big] from best_showing_seat()
                over players where pending(player)
                until (number of players where pending(player)) is 0
                   or ((number of players where can_act(player)) <= 1
                       and (number of players where can_act(player) and owes(player)) is 0)
        }
      }

      // 5th street (face up, upper limit).
      if (number of players where in_hand[player] and not folded[player]) > 1 {
        deal 1 card from deck to burn
        for each player p: if in_hand[p] and not folded[p] { deal 1 card from deck to upcards[p] }
        if (number of players where can_act(player)) >= 2 {
          run open_street(10, 0)
          round offering [check, bet, call, fold, raise] from best_showing_seat()
                over players where pending(player)
                until (number of players where pending(player)) is 0
                   or ((number of players where can_act(player)) <= 1
                       and (number of players where can_act(player) and owes(player)) is 0)
        }
      }

      // 6th street (face up, upper limit).
      if (number of players where in_hand[player] and not folded[player]) > 1 {
        deal 1 card from deck to burn
        for each player p: if in_hand[p] and not folded[p] { deal 1 card from deck to upcards[p] }
        if (number of players where can_act(player)) >= 2 {
          run open_street(10, 0)
          round offering [check, bet, call, fold, raise] from best_showing_seat()
                over players where pending(player)
                until (number of players where pending(player)) is 0
                   or ((number of players where can_act(player)) <= 1
                       and (number of players where can_act(player) and owes(player)) is 0)
        }
      }

      // 7th street (face DOWN, upper limit).
      if (number of players where in_hand[player] and not folded[player]) > 1 {
        deal 1 card from deck to burn
        for each player p: if in_hand[p] and not folded[p] { deal 1 card from deck to hole[p] }
        if (number of players where can_act(player)) >= 2 {
          run open_street(10, 0)
          round offering [check, bet, call, fold, raise] from best_showing_seat()
                over players where pending(player)
                until (number of players where pending(player)) is 0
                   or ((number of players where can_act(player)) <= 1
                       and (number of players where can_act(player) and owes(player)) is 0)
        }
      }

      // Showdown — RNG-free, decision-free. A contested hand reveals the
      // contenders' hole cards (public before the pot is judged; a lone
      // contender collects unrevealed). Each entrant then collects its
      // side-pot share — pot_share(p) is the committed-total layering, odd
      // chip to the first winner in seat order, uncalled remainder to the
      // best contender — and the hands leave play to the muck.
      if (number of players where in_hand[player] and not folded[player]) > 1 {
        for each player p: if in_hand[p] and not folded[p] {
          // Two steps so the merged seven land hole-first (hole, then board):
          // the muck below inherits that order, and the muck is what the next
          // hand's `move all cards to deck` + `shuffle` draw through — the
          // deal the RNG stream sees. The flip into the PublicHand is the
          // reveal: its movement event carries all seven identities.
          move all cards from upcards[p] to hole[p]
          move all cards from hole[p] to upcards[p]
        }
      }
      for each player p: if in_hand[p] {
        stack[p] := stack[p] + pot_share(p)
      }
      for each player p: if in_hand[p] {
        move all cards from hole[p] to muck
        move all cards from upcards[p] to muck
      }
    }
  }

  winner: highest stack
}

// Stud's own betting move. check/bet/call/raise and the can_act/owes/pending ring
// predicates come from `uses poker_betting` above; `fold` stays here because it
// touches Stud's zones — the folder's upcards go straight to the muck, so
// opponents stop seeing them, and that is an observation their information sets
// carry. All five are offered together in `offering [check, bet, call, fold,
// raise]` order; the `when:` guards filter to the exact option list per decision:
// free-to-act -> [check(, bet)], facing a bet -> [call, fold(, raise)].

move_type fold {
  when: bet_to_match > bet_by[actor]
  effect {
    folded[actor] := true
    move all cards from upcards[actor] to muck
  }
}

// Does this seat show a pair or better among its face-up cards? Two face-up
// cards of a rank is a pair showing; three is trips, which is "or better" and
// the same test. A folder's up cards are already in the muck, so this cannot
// see them. Factored as a function so the rank binder does not nest inside the
// player binder.
function up_rank_count(p : Player, r : Rank) = number of cards in upcards[p] where card.rank is r
function shows_pair(p : Player) = any rank where up_rank_count(p, rank) >= 2
